{
  "id": "27767_karu",
  "headword": "{狩|か}る",
  "reading": "かる",
  "romaji": "karu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to hunt; to catch (game)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to hunt; to catch (game)",
      "explanation": "To pursue and catch wild animals or birds, for food or sport. Also appears in fixed words for seasonal outings to enjoy nature."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27767_karu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{山|やま}で{鹿|しか}を{狩|か}る。",
      "english": "To hunt deer in the mountains.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27767_karu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{昔|むかし}、{人々|ひとびと}は{生|い}きるために{動物|どうぶつ}を{狩|か}った。",
      "english": "Long ago, people hunted animals in order to survive.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27767_karu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{鷹|たか}を{使|つか}って{野鳥|やちょう}を{狩|か}る{伝統|でんとう}が{今|いま}も{残|のこ}っている。",
      "english": "The tradition of hunting wild birds with hawks still survives today.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive godan verb. Xを{狩|か}る. The basic meaning is hunting wild animals or birds.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {獲物|えもの}を{狩|か}る: to hunt prey\n- 〜{狩|が}り: a seasonal outing to gather or enjoy something — {潮干狩|しおひが}り (clam digging), {紅葉狩|もみじが}り (autumn-leaf viewing), ぶどう{狩|が}り (grape picking)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {刈|か}る: to mow, to cut — same reading, different kanji; used for grass, crops, or hair\n- {捕|つか}まえる: to catch — catching without the pursuit or hunting nuance",
